<title>AFGHANISTAN: Bridas close to gas pipeline agreement.</title>
<headline>Bridas close to gas pipeline agreement.</headline>
<byline>Tim Johnston</byline>
<dateline>KABUL 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine oil and natural gas company Bridas is close to signing an agreement with the Taleban authorities in Afghanistan to build a gas pipeline from Turkmenistan through Afghanistan to Pakistan, a Bridas executive said on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;The final agreement is under discussion and we hope to sign by the end of the month.&quot; Mario Lopez Olaciregui, Managing Director of Bridas International Ltd, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Bridas is in competition with a consortium comprising Unocal of the United States and Delta Oil of Saudi Arabia to build the 1,250 km (780 mile) pipeline.</p>
<p>Lopez said that Bridas was putting together a consortium for the $2.5 billion project.</p>
<p>He said a Saudi Arabian company had already joined the consortium and three other companies had been invited to join; one from the United States, one from the European Community and a third from Southeast Asia.</p>
</text>
